First big concert of the year... probably my last... Isaiah Rashad.

Truly... My favourite artist of the new school.
Would not have missed this one for the world, what a performer....

And he is one... The pocket he sits in over a beat looks lazy on record, half asleep almost, but live it reveals itself for what it actually is... total control.
Every bar landing exactly where it needs to, the bounce holding steady even when the flow doubled up or folded back on itself mid-verse.
That is the part a recording cannot give you... watching someone ride a rhythm that precisely, in real time, no second take.

The lyrics do something different live too. On headphones you catch the wordplay once and move on.
In a crowd mouthing the same line back at him a beat before he says it, you hear exactly which lines landed,
which ones still sting, which ones are just fun to shout. The crowd mutates... becomes a part of him...
everyone pointing, without meaning to, at the bars that mattered to them.

Funny how I always thought I was one of a few that actually like his music... boy oh boy... the horde was out on this night...

Live music! Not better sound, not a better view, just that everyone at the concert decided,
independently, to show up for the same words at the same time. Does not get any better than that...

